\cf1\b VOICE OF DISABILITY\par
Reasonable Accommodation Request Template\b0\cf0\par
\fs20 Editable letter for South African workplaces and institutions\par\par
\b Date:\b0  [Day Month Year]\par
\b To:\b0  [Name / Human Resources / Manager]\par
\b Organisation:\b0  [Organisation name]\par\par
\b Subject: Request for reasonable accommodation\b0\par\par
Dear [Name],\par\par
I am requesting reasonable accommodation because I am experiencing a disability-related barrier that affects my ability to [describe the relevant task, process or part of participation].\par\par
The barrier I am experiencing is: [briefly describe the barrier in practical terms].\par\par
The adjustment that would help me participate on an equal basis is: [describe the accommodation you are requesting].\par\par
This adjustment would assist by: [briefly explain how it removes or reduces the barrier].\par\par
I am available to discuss this request and, if necessary, other accommodation options that would achieve the same result. Please confirm receipt of this request and let me know the next step in the process.\par\par
Please respond using [preferred communication method, if applicable].\par\par
Kind regards,\par
[Your name]\par
[Your preferred contact details]\par\par
\cf2\b Before you send it\b0\cf0\par
- Keep the request focused on the barrier and the solution.\par
- Save a copy of what you send and any response.\par
- Follow the organisation's formal accommodation process where practical.\par
- If your preferred adjustment is not possible, ask what alternative options were considered.\par\par
\b Important\b0\par
This general template is not legal advice. For a dispute, dismissal, discrimination complaint or legal deadline, seek appropriate professional advice.\par\par
Voice of Disability NPC | www.voiceofdisability.com\par
